Ethical use notice

NetSentinel is a defensive monitoring tool.  It captures packets on a network
interface, which means it can observe traffic that is not addressed to the
machine running it when the interface is in promiscuous mode.  You must only
run NetSentinel on:

  * Networks that you own, or
  * Networks on which you have explicit written authorisation to monitor.

Unauthorised packet capture may violate computer-misuse, wiretapping, privacy
and telecommunications laws in your jurisdiction.  The authors of NetSentinel
accept no liability for misuse of this software.